Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-01
Subject: Drop the charset/codepage path from the bootstrap compiler
License: expat

The 2.6.0 compiler reaches `charset` and the per-codepage unit tables
(cp437.pas, cp8859_1.pas, ...) for one purpose: convert non-UTF-8
source bytes into wide chars during lexing of widestring literals.  The
bootstrap target (compiling fpc itself) does not need that path at
runtime, but keeping it in the unit graph drags the charset tables into
the translated compiler.

Drop the dependency entirely.  In `widestr.pas`, remove the charset/cp*
unit imports and keep `asciichar2unicode`, `ascii2unicode`, and
`cpavailable` as byte-to-widechar bootstrap stubs so the surface stays
callable for `scandir.pas`'s `{$CodePage X}` directive handling.

In `options.pas`, remove `uses charset` and drop the `-Fm <name>`
`loadunicodemapping` handler since there is no longer a charset registry
to populate.

Source files using non-UTF-8 widestring literals will silently widen each
byte to its codepoint (identity for ASCII, lossy for non-ASCII).

--- a/compiler/widestr.pas
+++ b/compiler/widestr.pas
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
   interface
 
     uses
-       {$ifdef VER2_2}ccharset{$else VER2_2}charset{$endif VER2_2},globtype;
+       globtype;
 
 
